<p class="eyebrow">SWE-bench Multilingual &middot; rep30 &middot; measured 2026-08-02</p>
<h1>Where the code graph helps, and where the noise starts</h1>
<p class="lede">Per-language and per-repository token cost for <code>entire-graph</code> against a
no-tool baseline, for Sonnet and Opus at their best measured configurations. Negative is cheaper.</p>
</header>

<div class="alert">
<strong>Read the grey band before the bars.</strong> It is the measured noise floor: five runs of a
<em>byte-identical</em> configuration on the same instance differ by 34&ndash;262&nbsp;% in cost, and a control
group of 23 instances whose payload was provably never modified still moved 15 points. <strong>Every
bar that ends inside the grey band is indistinguishable from zero.</strong> Most of them do.
Language cells hold 1&ndash;4 instances and repository cells hold 1&ndash;2; they are shown because they were
asked for, not because they are individually resolvable.
</div>

